# Requisites on local host
    Clone the repository
    Run Docker desktop
    Deploy Kubernetes cluster inside the repository

# Deploying on Minikube
The project can be run manually step by step or by running a helper script

## With helper script
    chmod +x k8s/minikube/deploy_minikube.sh     # Changes file permission to make it executable
    ./k8s/minikube/deploy_minikube.sh            # Run the script 

    * Stop Minikube
    chmod +x k8s/minikube/stop_minikube.sh       # Changes file permission to make it executable
    ./k8s/minikube/stop_minikube.sh              # Delete the minikube cluster

## Manual execution

    minikube start                            # start MiniKube

    eval $(minikube docker-env)               # Point Docker CLI to Minikube’s Docker daemon

    docker build -t nasa-anomaly:latest .     # Build the image inside Minikube

    kubectl apply -f k8s/manifests/           # Apply Kubernetes manifests (PV, PVC, Deployment, Service)

    kubectl delete pod -l app=nasa-anomaly    # Restart pods to pick up the new image

    kubectl get pods                          # Check pod status

    minikube service cmapss-isolationforest   # Access the service (opens browser)



    delete Minikube                           # Delete minikube cluster



